**EXPERIMENT 13: Integrating JUnit Tests with Jenkins (Windows)**

---

## 🎯 **Objective**

To integrate JUnit test execution with Jenkins and generate test reports.

---

## 🧭 **Startup Guide (Windows System)**

### **Step 0: Start Jenkins**

```bat id="l3k2q1"
cd C:\Program Files\Jenkins
java -jar jenkins.war
```

👉 Open browser:

```id="z7x4c9"
http://localhost:8080
```

👉 Login

---

## ⚙️ **Execution Steps**

---

### **Step 1: Create Maven Project (JUnit Setup)**

```bat id="m1a8w2"
cd C:\Users\danis\OneDrive\Desktop
mvn archetype:generate -DgroupId=com.example -DartifactId=jenkins-junit -DarchetypeArtifactId=maven-archetype-quickstart -DinteractiveMode=false
cd jenkins-junit
```

---

### **Step 2: Replace pom.xml (FULL FILE)**

```xml id="p8z3k6"
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 
         http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">

    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>jenkins-junit</artifactId>
    <version>1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- JUnit 5 -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <version>5.10.0</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <!-- Surefire Plugin -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.2.5</version>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

</project>
```

---

### **Step 3: Create Java Class**

```bat id="t4n7v2"
notepad src\main\java\com\example\App.java
```

```java id="q9m1x5"
package com.example;

public class App {

    public int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }
}
```

---

### **Step 4: Create Test Class (Include Fail Case)**

```bat id="b6r2k9"
notepad src\test\java\com\example\AppTest.java
```

```java id="z3c7y1"
package com.example;

import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

public class AppTest {

    App app = new App();

    @Test
    void testAddPass() {
        assertEquals(5, app.add(2, 3));
    }

    @Test
    void testAddFail() {
        assertEquals(10, app.add(2, 3)); // intentional fail
    }
}
```

---

### **Step 5: Push Project to GitHub**

```bat id="x2w8k4"
git init
git add .
git commit -m "JUnit Jenkins integration"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/Daniishhhhh/jenkins-junit.git
git push -u origin main
```

---

### **Step 6: Create Jenkins Freestyle Job**

* Go to Jenkins → **New Item**
* Name: `junit-job`
* Select **Freestyle Project**
* Click **OK**

---

### **Step 7: Configure Git**

* Source Code Management → **Git**

```id="k7m2q8"
https://github.com/Daniishhhhh/jenkins-junit.git
```

👉 Branch:

```id="n2v6x1"
*/main
```

---

### **Step 8: Add Build Step**

👉 Build → Execute Windows batch command

```bat id="y5q8t2"
mvn test
```

---

### **Step 9: Add Post-Build Action (IMPORTANT)**

👉 Post-build Actions → **Publish JUnit test result report**

```id="u8k1z6"
target/surefire-reports/*.xml
```

---

### **Step 10: Save and Build**

* Click **Build Now**

---

## ❌ **Expected Output (With Fail Test)**

* Build Status: **FAILURE**
* Test Report shows:

```id="f9w3a7"
1 Passed, 1 Failed
```

---

### **Step 11: Fix Failed Test**

```java id="p6n4c2"
assertEquals(5, app.add(2, 3));
```

---

### **Step 12: Push Fix**

```bat id="r1m9x3"
git add .
git commit -m "Fixed test"
git push
```

---

### **Step 13: Build Again**

* Click **Build Now**

---

## ✅ **Expected Output (After Fix)**

* Build Status: **SUCCESS**
* Test Report:

```id="v7t2k9"
2 Passed, 0 Failed
```

